<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-10.25%" pitch="-2.25%">
            Abraham was old, well advanced in years, and the Lord had blessed him in all things.<break time="500ms"/>
      Sarah, his wife, had died, and Isaac was grown, but he had no wife.<break time="500ms"/>
      Abraham called the oldest servant of his house, the one who managed all that he had, and said to him, put your hand under my thigh and swear to me.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Do not take a wife for my son from the daughters of the Canaanites among whom I dwell.<break time="500ms"/>
      Go to my country, to my kindred, and take a wife for my son Isaac.<break time="1000ms"/>
      The servant asked, what if the woman is not willing to follow me to this land?<break time="500ms"/>
      Shall I take your son back to the land from which you came?<break time="500ms"/>
      Abraham said, do not take my son back there.<break time="500ms"/>
      The Lord God of heaven, who took me from my father's house, He will send His angel before you.<break time="1000ms"/>
      It was a promise built on decades of faithfulness.<break time="500ms"/>
      Abraham had walked with God through impossible things, and now he trusted that same God with his son's future.<break time="1800ms"/>
      So the servant took ten camels from the camels of his master, and departed.<break time="500ms"/>
      He carried with him all manner of good things, gifts from Abraham's wealth.<break time="500ms"/>
      And he set out on the long road to Mesopotamia, to the city of Nahor.<break time="1000ms"/>
      The journey was slow and steady, across dust and distance.<break time="500ms"/>
      A mission of trust, carried forward by obedience.<break time="1800ms"/>
      You can rest as the servant travels.<break time="3800ms"/>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
